--[[
        THE WASHROOM -- under DOORS' Hotel- (the Hotel before Hotel+): the laundry, and past B-02 the attic

            loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bonellocristian78-lab/Gradish-Mode/claude/sei-qui-con-noi-ye4k62/Washroom"))()

        Run it in room 0. Beside its door (0001) the floor opens: a railing, a sign, and a staircase going down in the
        Hotel's own style. You walk down it: no teleport.

        B-01, a door of DOORS' own (a copy of room 0's), opens on THE WASHROOM: tiles below, the Hotel's wallpaper and trim
        above, its pillars with DOORS' lamps on them, DOORS' windows high on the walls (the rain on them, the lightning of
        DOORS' own storm), a bank of stacked dryers, two rows of washers back to back (some running a wash), DOORS' dressers,
        shelves, carts and clock, pipes under the ceiling, a flooded floor. B-02 at the far end has DOORS' lock on it.
        Somewhere on the pipes a valve drains the water: then something shines in the big drain. The key (B-02 on its tag)
        goes into your inventory, DOORS' own hotbar: hold it (1), unlock the lock, it opens and falls as DOORS' locks do.

        Past B-02, up a few steps, THE ATTIC: worn floorboards, dark wood walls, beams, DOORS' chandeliers, a rug, a table
        with its chairs, DOORS' fireplace burning (its armchair before it), its sideboard, painting, globe, its dressers and
        its tables with drawers, bookcases, grandfather clock, couch and chairs, three of DOORS' wardrobes, luggage piled
        up, the key board of the lobby, DOORS' chests, barrels and crates, furniture under sheets, DOORS' windows. B-03 is
        locked too: its key is somewhere up there. Then stairs, and through the last door you are back in room 0.

        DOORS' own systems: its doors swing on their own hinges (their servo, their knob turning), its locks open their
        shackle and fall, its drawers slide out on their own rails (and close again), its keys and flashlight are items
        in its hotbar, its wardrobes open on their own animations, its desk bell rings with its own animation; its
        location titles, tips, captions, prompts; its lamps flickering as DOORS flickers them; its lightning; its
